# Production load balancer: inbound HTTPS from CloudFront only.
#
# The load balancer uses a security group that Elastic Beanstalk does not
# create: sg-06ef22abcfaf6c8df (seizeapp-env-node22-alb-cloudfront-only,
# us-east-1, vpc-0049175e3bed48694). Its only inbound rule is TCP 443 from the
# AWS-managed CloudFront origin-facing prefix list (pl-3b927c52); its only
# outbound rule is TCP 3001 to the instances.
#
# With ManagedSecurityGroup set, Elastic Beanstalk does not create its own
# load balancer group (which allowed 80 and 443 from 0.0.0.0/0), adds no
# inbound rules to this one, and lets the instances accept TCP 3001 from it.
# A throwaway environment in this VPC confirmed all three before production
# switched on 2026-11-06.
#
# These settings were applied to seizeapp-env-node22 with update-environment.
# This file records them so a rebuilt environment gets the same group; values
# set through the API take precedence over it.
#
# Port 80 has no inbound rule. The HTTP listener from redirection.config still
# exists but is unreachable. CloudFront connects to the origin over HTTPS only
# and redirects viewers from HTTP to HTTPS itself. The prefix list counts as 55
# of the group's 60 inbound rules, so it can be allowed on one port only.
#
# Scope: only seizeapp-env-node22 (us-east-1) processes this file. Staging
# deploys through SSM to a plain instance and ignores .ebextensions. The group
# ID exists only in us-east-1.
#
# The prefix list admits every CloudFront distribution. The secret
# X-Origin-Verify header, required by the HTTPS listener and sent only by
# E3KTTDJUNHRYW9, limits the origin to this distribution. Its value stays out of
# the repository; see ops/scripts/production-origin-lock.sh.
#
# Rollback: run `ops/scripts/production-origin-lock.sh unlock` for direct
# traffic now. To return to the Elastic Beanstalk group, revert this file and
# remove both options with update-environment --options-to-remove.
# Runbook: ops/docs/developer/cloudfront-page-cache.md
option_settings:
  aws:elbv2:loadbalancer:
    SecurityGroups: sg-06ef22abcfaf6c8df
    ManagedSecurityGroup: sg-06ef22abcfaf6c8df
